; The dev zone's INITIAL state — deliberately almost empty.
;
; Nothing here names a host. Every A/AAAA/CNAME this zone ends up holding was written by
; Stratt through RFC 2136, which is what makes the live proof falsifiable: if the record
; is there, the plugin put it there, because it started with an SOA and an NS and nothing
; else. A seeded record would make "the name resolves" pass for the wrong reason.
$TTL 300
@   IN  SOA ns.__ZONE__. hostmaster.__ZONE__. (
        1          ; serial — named bumps it on every dynamic update
        3600       ; refresh
        600        ; retry
        604800     ; expire
        300 )      ; negative TTL
@   IN  NS  ns.__ZONE__.
ns  IN  A   127.0.0.1
